  "series": [
    {
      "patch": "/Volumes/vaEVAS-runs/pr-review-20261025/grill-vams-2023/capability-batch1-r2-fixes-opus-20261028/r3/series/0001-Read-the-registered-baseline-kernel-variables-in-the.patch",
      "patch_sha256": "c84588a87291540552dc54c3b4f04123c42d508f4382ea260e47f2b14af2f459",
      "commit": "a8225ba0a9518f252266c299a2c59a4d6ac9f64a",
      "tree": "b7b612b30e884b874ddcebbf618f63c9734dcfe0",
      "paths": [
        "evas/tests/test_proof_work_limit.py"
      ],
      "message": "Read the registered baseline kernel variables in the two main-kernel checks\n\nEVAS_TEST_MAIN_KERNEL was not a registered CI environment input, so\ntest_every_literal_python_environment_consumer_is_registered failed. The two\nold-kernel checks now read EVAS_TEST_BASELINE_KERNEL and EVAS_TEST_BASELINE_SHA256,\nwhich scripts/ci_evidence.py already registers, and require both to be the release\nkernel built from main d6b7543f (SHA-256 061c9c8e...), checked before and after the\nrun. test_history_forcing reads the same variables for the C8 baseline kernel; the\npinned SHA-256 tells the two apart, so a C8 kernel fails these checks instead of\nstanding in for main."
    },
    {
      "patch": "/Volumes/vaEVAS-runs/pr-review-20261025/grill-vams-2023/capability-batch1-r2-fixes-opus-20261028/r3/series/0002-Fail-the-by-name-RC-check-when-a-check-ends-early-or.patch",
      "patch_sha256": "b3f834c66db8294d12dc7b219692c2e43fd4fd2e82029dd2dd4c0db624679bf6",
      "commit": "4b16143ac5413622df676b476cce7c8a80d91197",
      "tree": "5a9e6053090cbba22dd78463a209470783e8cf5d",
      "paths": [
        ".github/workflows/numerical-assurance.yml",
        "evas/capabilities/README.md",
        "scripts/run_explicit_checks.py",
        "scripts/tests/test_ci_inventory.py",
        "scripts/tests/test_explicit_checks.py",
        "scripts/verify_explicit_checks.py"
      ],
      "message": "Fail the by-name RC check when a check ends early or leaves no complete receipt\n\nR1-ST-02: a checked module that called sys.exit(0) on import made the runner exit\n0 with no receipt and zero executions. Each check now runs in its own process with\nseparate import, load and run phases; SystemExit with any status, KeyboardInterrupt\nor any other BaseException, and a process that dies without a result (os._exit),\nare recorded as not_completed and fail the run. The receipt is always written and\nrecords the method id, executed count, outcome, module SHA-256 and the SHA-256 of\nevery required file variable (the kernels), read before and after the run.\nIn rust-regression a new step runs scripts/verify_explicit_checks.py, which reads\nonly the receipt and fails unless every named check executed exactly once with\noutcome ok and the kernel digest recorded; the receipt upload now uses\nif-no-files-found: error."
    },
    {
      "patch": "/Volumes/vaEVAS-runs/pr-review-20261025/grill-vams-2023/capability-batch1-r2-fixes-opus-20261028/r3/series/0003-Reject-an-explicit-null-proof_work_limit-in-a-CLI-ma.patch",
      "patch_sha256": "af53e94af4b6517e019ebd4f7c9186947b992a74faa8a9b795327d469018ad1b",
      "commit": "5669af2208f329776ecc262f66e7326cd17a9955",
      "tree": "0cac816c226babdf1b6e011e03ba6b98358213eb",
      "paths": [
        "evas/capabilities/test_requirement_links.py",
        "evas/docs/reference/proof-work-limit.md",
        "evas/src/evas/manifest.py",
        "evas/tests/test_proof_work_limit.py"
      ],
      "message": "Reject an explicit null proof_work_limit in a CLI manifest\n\nR1-SP-01: \"proof_work_limit\": null in a transient manifest became Python None, was\nread as unset and silently ran with the default 1e9, while the same null sent to\nthe kernel is invalid_inputs. The shared manifest schema now tells a missing field\nfrom a present one: a present transient.proof_work_limit must be an exact integer\nin 1..1e13, and null or any other shape is rejected while the manifest is read\n(manifest_input, naming the field), before anything is sent. None in the Python API\nkeeps meaning unset; proof-work-limit.md states the three layers. Two collected\ntests, one without a kernel and one control with a missing field or an integer,\nare added to the batch-1 link inventory."
    },
    {
      "patch": "/Volumes/vaEVAS-runs/pr-review-20261025/grill-vams-2023/capability-batch1-r2-fixes-opus-20261028/r3/series/0004-Update-the-batch-1-cards-for-the-r3-fixes.patch",
      "patch_sha256": "5ff499f8d59b13fee37280ed91ac4d81ca5e82e90bdf8dad36d801a207d4d117",
      "commit": "6fd50bda4907296767d551a9de4c593b6c749fbe",
      "tree": "3833d06666e41344bd4172af51962266d9fd8766",
      "paths": [
        "evas/capabilities/data/registry.json"
      ],
      "message": "Update the batch-1 cards for the r3 fixes\n\nrequirement:proof-work-limit cites main-kernel-checks-r3-final.json, the main-kernel\nchecks rerun on the final tree with the registered baseline variables, and states\nthe three layers for an invalid value: JSON null in a kernel request is\ninvalid_inputs, null in a CLI manifest is rejected before sending, and None in the\nPython API means unset. The two manifest tests join case:proof-work-limit-python.\nBoth cards depend on the changed contract document, so every reference is\nrecomputed; versions stay 1."
    }
  ],
